WEBVTT

00:46.310 --> 00:49.030
Foolish humans!

00:49.030 --> 00:52.610
Mere mortals cannot possibly defeat me!

00:58.000 --> 00:59.370
<i>The Shadow Worlds.</i>

00:59.370 --> 01:03.880
<i>They represent the worst calamity 
humanity has ever faced.</i>

01:04.540 --> 01:10.160
<i>They're steadily shrouding our 
world in black fog.</i>

01:11.010 --> 01:14.110
<i>We have no way of knowing
 what goes on inside that fog.</i>

01:15.430 --> 01:17.680
<i>The one thing we do know</i>

01:17.680 --> 01:23.320
<i>is that no living creature can 
survive in the land it taints.</i>

01:25.830 --> 01:28.840
<i>There's only one way to save the world.</i>

01:28.840 --> 01:33.580
<i>Before the fog claims everything, 
we must conquer the Shadow Worlds.</i>

01:34.950 --> 01:37.780
Let's settle this once and for all,
 Boromir Napolitan!

01:37.780 --> 01:42.410
I will slay you and bring 
an end to this accursed hell!

01:48.540 --> 01:49.680
Here it comes!

01:49.800 --> 01:53.390
<b>  Destruction</b>

01:49.800 --> 01:53.390
<b></b>Episode 1

02:07.990 --> 02:09.150
What?

02:11.450 --> 02:12.630
Well, then...

02:31.840 --> 02:33.180
What?!

02:34.020 --> 02:36.390
Magical pattern analysis complete!

02:36.390 --> 02:39.140
I've sealed every Draconian spell!

02:39.140 --> 02:40.180
Good!

02:39.140 --> 02:41.070
Nice, Desir!

02:44.230 --> 02:46.160
How impudent!

02:46.160 --> 02:51.860
Measly humans, trying to stand in my way?!

03:01.860 --> 03:03.420
You bastards!

03:14.330 --> 03:17.010
How dare you?!

03:31.400 --> 03:34.670
Here's the rest of our magic power.
 Take it all!

03:41.380 --> 03:43.500
Now!

03:55.580 --> 03:58.810
Curse you!

03:59.940 --> 04:06.010
This cannot be where I meet my end!

04:08.210 --> 04:09.650
We did it!

04:13.320 --> 04:14.320
Good!

04:21.660 --> 04:26.510
Finally... we can get out of this hell.

04:33.170 --> 04:35.860
Great work, everyone!

04:35.860 --> 04:38.260
Now the world is saved!

04:38.670 --> 04:41.000
"Cleared" message, late.

04:41.000 --> 04:43.100
Wrong target?

04:43.470 --> 04:47.600
No, the slaying of Boromir Napolitan 
should definitely do it.

04:48.670 --> 04:50.600
Right?

04:50.600 --> 04:55.780
We'd usually be sent 
back to our world by now.

04:56.230 --> 04:58.210
Let's give it a little more time.

04:58.790 --> 05:01.240
Everything is over now.

05:01.730 --> 05:02.990
You're right.

05:05.710 --> 05:09.400
Of the one hundred and fifty
 million people who fought him,

05:09.400 --> 05:11.160
only six of us survived.

05:11.610 --> 05:12.970
It's hard to believe.

05:16.490 --> 05:17.620
<i>That's right.</i>

05:18.330 --> 05:20.870
<i>This world took too much from us.</i>

05:22.420 --> 05:24.420
<i>The comrades I fought alongside...</i>

05:25.370 --> 05:27.240
<i>My irreplaceable friends...</i>

05:29.050 --> 05:33.230
<i>This hellscape has taken too much from us.</i>

05:35.860 --> 05:38.170
We've finally defeated Napolitan.

05:38.670 --> 05:41.030
Let's talk about something uplifting.

05:41.480 --> 05:44.300
You can't look away from reality.

05:44.300 --> 05:47.570
Ninety-nine percent of the mages died.

05:47.930 --> 05:50.660
We need to think about what's to come.

05:51.990 --> 05:54.910
Before that, we must pray.

05:57.820 --> 05:58.930
Come on, now.

05:58.930 --> 06:01.790
We saved the world, so let's not fight.

06:09.020 --> 06:13.110
Rafaello, you did an amazing job 
of blocking Napolitan's attacks,

06:13.110 --> 06:14.760
as expected of the knight of light.

06:14.760 --> 06:16.300
Not at all.

06:16.300 --> 06:20.270
This time, Desir contributed 
much more to the victory.

06:21.900 --> 06:23.380
Yes.

06:23.380 --> 06:27.230
No Desir, no clear.

06:27.230 --> 06:28.240
Thank you.

06:28.790 --> 06:31.320
Oh, please.

06:32.240 --> 06:37.680
I must confess that I didn't think 
 you could withstand this fight.

06:37.680 --> 06:38.750
What?

06:39.120 --> 06:41.590
Even with the protective artifact,

06:41.590 --> 06:46.960
to analyze and seal Napolitan's 
Draconian spells with your Circle...

06:47.620 --> 06:49.970
Even I do not possess such power.

06:50.930 --> 06:55.740
Despite having so much strength, 
you were absolutely unknown.

06:56.500 --> 06:58.020
Why is that?

06:58.750 --> 07:00.630
I'd like to know, as well.

07:01.680 --> 07:03.110
Because...

07:04.060 --> 07:05.890
I'm a commoner.

07:07.770 --> 07:08.930
How unfortunate.

07:08.930 --> 07:13.220
If you'd been at the Magic Tower, I could 
have given you any support you needed.

07:17.960 --> 07:23.680
By the way, do you all know what you'll
 do once we get back to our world?

07:26.070 --> 07:28.850
My dead friends' homes. Visit.

07:28.850 --> 07:30.760
Their keepsakes. Return.

07:31.180 --> 07:35.540
Their honorable deaths. Remember. Forever.

07:37.880 --> 07:40.760
I will go back to the League 
of Western Kingdoms.

07:41.390 --> 07:43.560
I'll take care of the victims' families,

07:43.560 --> 07:49.270
and I'll build a memorial and a temple 
for the spirits of those who died here.

07:50.050 --> 07:53.150
We have to prevent a recurrence
 of Shadow Worlds.

07:53.540 --> 07:59.280
If one of a similar scale to this appears,
 it really will be the end of us.

07:59.980 --> 08:01.500
How about you, Azest?

08:10.910 --> 08:12.420
You, Desir?

08:12.840 --> 08:15.590
Are you returning to Hebrion Academy?

08:17.790 --> 08:19.000
I...

08:21.600 --> 08:23.990
We used to have a villa around here.

08:25.130 --> 08:31.820
Every evening, the sea sparkled like gold. 
It was beautiful.

08:31.820 --> 08:35.510
I don't... want to die here.

08:35.510 --> 08:37.410
This...

08:37.410 --> 08:40.370
This isn't... right...

08:48.630 --> 08:51.210
I'll think about it for a while.

08:59.660 --> 09:00.580
What was that?!

09:01.740 --> 09:04.180
It isn't over yet?!

09:04.670 --> 09:06.810
What is this magic power?

09:06.810 --> 09:08.810
He's still alive.

09:09.220 --> 09:10.710
That can't be.

09:10.710 --> 09:13.280
I know we killed him.

09:18.250 --> 09:20.870
Wait... the dragon's heart!

09:21.320 --> 09:22.950
You know what's going on?

09:23.510 --> 09:25.940
I have read about it in an old document.

09:26.320 --> 09:28.990
Dragon hearts don't only pump blood.

09:28.990 --> 09:33.920
They also store and circulate 
vast amounts of mana.

09:35.620 --> 09:37.950
When the dragon dies, the blood stops,

09:37.950 --> 09:40.540
and the stored mama, with nowhere else to go...

09:41.050 --> 09:45.080
You mean the mana Napolitan 
stored up will explode?!

09:45.990 --> 09:47.250
No way!

09:56.650 --> 10:00.950
Why couldn't you realize that 
before we killed him?!

10:01.640 --> 10:06.300
This is the first time in history 
that humans have defeated a dragon.

10:11.250 --> 10:13.130
An extraordinary amount of magic power!

10:13.130 --> 10:16.120
Even in perfect condition, 
we couldn't stop it!

10:20.590 --> 10:21.960
It's useless.

10:21.960 --> 10:24.770
That's a ball of pure magic power.

10:24.770 --> 10:26.900
Your spells won't work.

10:30.650 --> 10:34.950
Unfortunately, we all must 
prepare for the end.

10:39.860 --> 10:42.820
No... then this world is...

10:43.520 --> 10:44.720
How regrettable.

10:45.400 --> 10:48.040
My lord... My god...

10:56.730 --> 10:58.540
<i>Is this really it?</i>

11:03.690 --> 11:04.760
<i>I...</i>

11:05.830 --> 11:06.990
<i>I...</i>

11:08.260 --> 11:11.000
<i>I...!</i>

11:42.920 --> 11:43.800
What?

11:48.470 --> 11:50.760
What's going on here?

11:51.810 --> 11:54.180
What's happening?

12:13.350 --> 12:17.460
New students, welcome to Hebrion Academy.

12:20.180 --> 12:21.770
Is that a professor?

12:21.770 --> 12:23.260
She's beautiful...

12:24.820 --> 12:27.680
You there, no chitchat.

12:29.780 --> 12:30.930
Yes, ma'am!

12:32.670 --> 12:34.460
Professor Brigitte...

12:36.130 --> 12:39.920
I'm sorry to tell you 
after you came all this way,

12:39.920 --> 12:43.570
but not everyone here can be enrolled.

12:43.570 --> 12:45.070
Huh?

12:45.920 --> 12:51.990
You will now take a test.
 Only the top 600 will be accepted.

12:52.690 --> 12:54.530
There's a test?

12:54.530 --> 12:56.210
I didn't know that.

12:56.490 --> 12:58.150
The test is...

13:01.180 --> 13:03.720
to clear a Shadow World.

13:06.440 --> 13:09.520
A Shadow World... That's impossible.

13:09.520 --> 13:10.920
It's too dangerous.

13:12.180 --> 13:14.470
There's no need to be afraid.

13:20.650 --> 13:21.980
This can't be real.

13:21.980 --> 13:27.990
This Shadow World is an artificial one 
created for the purpose of the test.

13:28.480 --> 13:29.920
<i>What's going on?!</i>

13:30.480 --> 13:35.500
You will hear more from your seniors, 
who will support you in the process.

13:36.610 --> 13:37.740
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

13:39.330 --> 13:40.500
<i>This is...</i>

13:41.210 --> 13:47.010
Let us now begin the entrance 
exam for the year 3613.

14:11.810 --> 14:14.400
Hebrion Academy's entrance ceremony?

14:15.900 --> 14:17.160
It can't be!

14:21.950 --> 14:27.300
<i>The battle against Boromir 
Napolitan started in 3616.</i>

14:28.500 --> 14:33.720
<i>And for the next ten years, 
we fought in that dungeon and...</i>

14:37.000 --> 14:38.860
<i>everything was destroyed.</i>

14:45.000 --> 14:48.170
<i>Then, our fight...</i>

14:49.250 --> 14:50.750
<i>That hell we went through...</i>

14:54.510 --> 14:56.600
<i>What was the point of it?!</i>

15:17.520 --> 15:18.980
<i>This isn't a dream.</i>

15:20.510 --> 15:23.860
<i>I clearly remember this view.</i>

15:25.090 --> 15:26.540
<i>All of it.</i>

15:29.820 --> 15:30.940
<i>This is...</i>

15:33.030 --> 15:35.420
Hey! I was looking for you!

15:36.950 --> 15:40.490
I couldn't find you at the meeting spot.

15:40.790 --> 15:42.420
You're Desir Herrman, right?

15:42.870 --> 15:45.000
Oh, I'm sorry...

15:46.200 --> 15:48.300
Well, it's all right.

15:49.000 --> 15:51.280
I'm Ladoria Doriche.

15:51.280 --> 15:55.180
I'm a second-year student here, 
and I'll be your mentor.

15:56.690 --> 15:59.600
Nice to meet you, Ms. Doriche.

15:59.600 --> 16:01.350
Call me Ladoria.

16:01.350 --> 16:02.500
Nice to meet you.

16:04.240 --> 16:05.870
<i>Ladoria Doriche.</i>

16:06.830 --> 16:09.640
<i>She's a genius of a mage 
who wields fire magic.</i>

16:09.640 --> 16:13.940
<i>If I remember correctly, she 
placed first in the academy rankings.</i>

16:14.500 --> 16:16.380
Hmm? Something wrong?

16:16.380 --> 16:18.710
Oh, nothing.

16:18.710 --> 16:21.790
Just... nervous.

16:22.110 --> 16:24.550
Oh, about the test?

16:25.810 --> 16:28.250
Don't be nervous!

16:28.630 --> 16:32.050
It's a Shadow World created for the test.

16:32.050 --> 16:33.800
Is that so?

16:33.800 --> 16:38.340
Yes, just to see if you can fight.

16:39.160 --> 16:42.180
Huh? Are you a commoner?

16:42.590 --> 16:45.190
I don't believe that's
 a problem for enrollment?

16:45.550 --> 16:47.510
It's not, but...

16:48.170 --> 16:51.440
Even if you pass, you'll be 
in the beta class.

16:52.420 --> 16:53.700
<i>I know.</i>

16:55.030 --> 16:57.280
<i>This school has a discriminatory practice.</i>

16:57.990 --> 17:01.340
<i>It puts nobles into the alpha class, 
and commoners into the beta class.</i>

17:02.030 --> 17:07.290
<i>Even if you have talent, you can't receive a 
proper education if you're a commoner.</i>

17:08.340 --> 17:12.360
<i>It's crushed the talents of many mages.</i>

17:18.230 --> 17:22.310
Well, if you can't pass the test, 
you can't enroll here anyhow...

17:29.050 --> 17:31.530
<i>ID pass, confirmed.</i>

17:31.530 --> 17:34.400
<i>Welcome, Ms. Ladoria Doriche.</i>

17:35.070 --> 17:36.570
Come on in.

17:51.380 --> 17:53.600
Huh? You're not surprised?

17:55.600 --> 17:58.720
I've seen a similar building before...

17:59.100 --> 18:00.720
That can't be true!

18:00.720 --> 18:03.690
There's no facility this grand anywhere else.

18:07.900 --> 18:10.680
Come on, we'll be late. Hurry!

18:15.430 --> 18:16.740
Ladoria.

18:20.850 --> 18:23.200
Hey, fancy seeing you here.

18:24.020 --> 18:25.910
Do you know him?

18:25.910 --> 18:28.800
He's an annoying jerk called Elheim.

18:30.560 --> 18:33.900
<i>I think he's a mage who wields water magic,</i>

18:33.900 --> 18:36.180
<i>and who doesn't get along with Ladoria.</i>

18:37.610 --> 18:39.180
You don't like him, then?

18:39.180 --> 18:41.320
"Don't like" is putting it mildly.

18:41.320 --> 18:42.760
I hate him!

18:43.560 --> 18:45.310
It took you a while to get here, huh?

18:45.310 --> 18:48.560
Oh, you're slow because you're short.

18:48.560 --> 18:50.760
You are as aggravating as ever.

18:50.760 --> 18:53.520
Your tongue reveals your crude upbringing.

18:53.520 --> 18:58.610
Just what one expects a despicable 
fire mage like yourself to say.

18:58.610 --> 19:02.240
And who lost to that despicable fire mage?

19:02.240 --> 19:05.740
You can't tell the difference between 
losing and letting someone win?

19:05.740 --> 19:06.910
I know, right?!

19:06.910 --> 19:08.740
Because if that was you going all-out,

19:08.740 --> 19:11.730
you'd be far too ashamed to still be here!

19:16.310 --> 19:19.010
Hey. Are you Ladoria's...?

19:19.320 --> 19:21.080
Yes, I am.

19:21.800 --> 19:24.430
You seem to know some manners.

19:24.430 --> 19:25.430
Your name?

19:25.820 --> 19:27.550
I'm Desir Herrman.

19:36.960 --> 19:39.610
Man, you're a commoner?!

19:39.610 --> 19:41.780
As expected of you, Ladoria!

19:44.460 --> 19:46.660
That'll be no competition at all.

19:46.660 --> 19:48.120
What do you mean?

19:49.970 --> 19:52.520
Just look forward to the test.

19:57.850 --> 20:00.800
Oh, a word of advice.

20:02.170 --> 20:06.790
Even if you get lucky and pass the test, 
you'll end up in the beta class.

20:07.200 --> 20:09.560
You might be better off not taking it.

20:10.710 --> 20:12.310
That's all.

20:12.890 --> 20:15.030
Look forward to what?!

20:15.030 --> 20:18.250
Spit it out! Ugh!

20:19.800 --> 20:23.070
<i>The entrance exam will commence shortly.</i>

20:23.070 --> 20:27.220
<i>Candidates, please come to the testing site.</i>

20:27.910 --> 20:29.310
Shall we go?

20:30.720 --> 20:32.110
Let's go!

20:32.890 --> 20:35.880
Listen! You've got to pass the test, okay?!

20:36.170 --> 20:37.880
You hear me?!

20:38.570 --> 20:40.980
I-I'll do what I can...

20:51.510 --> 20:56.100
<i>All the people and places I knew...</i>

20:58.290 --> 21:00.340
<i>This really is my past.</i>

21:01.970 --> 21:04.820
<i>If so, then perhaps...</i>

21:11.170 --> 21:12.470
<i>Perhaps...</i>

21:19.910 --> 21:21.180
Not here, huh?

21:22.510 --> 21:23.980
Hey, you.

21:29.220 --> 21:32.260
Why do you keep looking all around like that?

21:32.260 --> 21:34.700
Can't you settle down? It's embarrassing.

21:36.610 --> 21:38.980
R-Romantica.

21:51.620 --> 21:53.790
<i>I don't know why this happened.</i>

21:54.550 --> 21:55.660
<i>But...</i>

21:56.570 --> 21:59.200
<i>I won't let that tragedy repeat itself.</i>

22:00.420 --> 22:02.990
<i>I will rewrite the history of the world!</i>

22:19.830 --> 22:27.100
<i>Fate is always more heroic than any story</i>

22:29.370 --> 22:36.150
<i>The one and only despair flaunts 
a completely different sky</i>

22:36.150 --> 22:38.600
<i>A stolen smile</i>

22:38.600 --> 22:48.230
<i>Put a period on the nights 
of lament and depression</i>

22:48.230 --> 22:52.650
<i>When the season comes around 
for the second time, gear yourself up</i>

22:52.650 --> 22:57.060
<i>For the final challenge</i>

22:57.060 --> 23:00.490
<i>Why don't we struggle, cry, and bloom away?</i>

23:00.490 --> 23:06.740
<i>I have a future, a future I want to 
go back to no matter what it takes</i>

23:06.740 --> 23:10.100
<i>Here we go and embrace 
the next life, nice to meet you</i>

23:10.100 --> 23:17.280
<i>There's a world, a world 
I want to repaint with you</i>

23:17.280 --> 23:19.440
<i>Let's go see the end together</i>

23:19.440 --> 23:22.120
<i>The ending credits signal the beginning</i>

23:22.120 --> 23:26.830
<i>A special story drawn by light and shadow</i>

23:26.830 --> 23:29.220
<i>Ge ge ge ge ge get back</i>

23:29.220 --> 23:31.930
<i>To my own story</i>

23:35.470 --> 23:39.930
<b>    The Test</b>

23:35.470 --> 23:39.930
<b></b>Episode 2

23:35.530 --> 23:37.680
Next episode: "The Test."
